*.woff2 binary

# Fork-and-sync ours-policies — CONFLICT-TIME DEFENSE ONLY.
# `merge=ours` drivers do not fire on one-sided changes: if base alone changes
# one of these files and a fork hasn't re-touched it since its last sync, git
# resolves cleanly and the fork silently takes base's version. The sync flow
# (quartz-sync `sync`, or the manual interim procedure) must additionally
# restore-ours fork-identity paths (README.md, content/index.md) after each
# merge. Lockfile/.node-version flowing in one-sided is desired.
content/index.md merge=ours
README.md merge=ours
package-lock.json merge=ours
.node-version merge=ours
